1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,760
With the same grades, immigrant kids,
especially boys,

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:06,800
choose vocational school
much more often.

3
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:09,880
Compared with Italian students,
it's a huge gap,

4
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:12,520
reaching up to
16 percentage points.

5
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:17,000
An experiment involved 70 middle
schools out of 145

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,180
drawn by lot
to study the problem.

7
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:22,920
The programme offered
psychological guidance

8
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:25,500
and tutoring for the
best immigrant students.

9
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:30,200
The real obstacle to overcome
wasn't actual ability,

10
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:34,100
but invisible psychological barriers
that lowered expectations.

11
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:35,900
The results are clear.

12
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:38,980
Boys in the programme are 12% more likely

13
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:41,720
to choose academic or technical school
instead of vocational.

14
00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:43,800
For this same group, moreover,

15
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:47,320
grade retention drops
sharply, by 44%.

16
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:49,660
For girls, no effect,

17
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:52,840
simply because for them
this initial gap didn't exist.

18
00:00:53,060 --> 00:00:55,320
The moral of the experiment is clear.

19
00:00:55,460 --> 00:00:58,620
Early guidance breaks down
psychological barriers

20
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:01,200
and frees true talent.
